{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T16:06:32.780627", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # You are provided with an environment instance and a primitive name.\n  # The function should return a list of actions (integers from 0-4) to take the agent\n  # to the specified primitive.\n\n  # This is a complex problem that involves pathfinding, inventory management,\n  # and tool usage. Here's a breakdown of how you might approach it:\n  # 1. Identify where the primitive is in the environment.\n  # 2. Check if the agent can reach it directly, or if it needs tools (like BRIDGE).\n  # 3. If needed, use available tools from inventory to create paths.\n  # 4. Navigate to the primitive and collect it.\n\n  # You may need to use:\n  # - env._current_state.next_to(primitive_index)\n  # - env._current_state.features_dict()\n  # - env._current_state.pos\n  # - env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  # - env._current_state.grid\n  # - env._current_state.inventory\n\n  pass", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
