{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:18:17.206040", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Your code here\n  # This function should return a list of actions to collect the specified primitive.\n  # You can use the environment's state and methods to determine the path.\n\n  # Get the current state of the environment\n  state = env._current_state\n  world = state.world\n  scenario = state.scenario\n\n  # Find the index of the primitive\n  primitive_index = world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Check if we already have the primitive in inventory\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Find all positions where the primitive is located\n  primitive_positions = []\n  for y in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n      for x in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n          if state.grid[x, y, primitive_index] == 1:\n              primitive_positions.append((x, y))\n\n  # If we found a position, try to move there\n  if primitive_positions:\n      target_pos = primitive_positions[0]\n      actions = []\n      \n      # Calculate the path from current position to target position\n      current_pos = state.pos\n      \n      # Simple pathfinding: move towards target\n      while current_pos != target_pos:\n          x_diff = target_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n          y_diff = target_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n          \n          if abs(x_diff) > abs(y_diff):\n              if x_diff > 0:\n                  actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n                  current_pos = (current_pos[0] + 1, current_pos[1])\n              else:\n                  actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n                  current_pos = (current_pos[0] - 1, current_pos[1])\n          else:\n              if y_diff > 0:\n                  actions.append(1)  # DOWN\n                  current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] + 1)\n              else:\n                  actions.append(0)  # UP\n                  current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] - 1)\n      \n      # Add the action to collect the primitive\n      actions.append(4)  # USE\n      \n      return actions\n\n  # If no primitive found, return empty list\n  return []", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 1.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:18:19.154857", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index for the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get the current state\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Check if we already have the primitive\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Find all locations in the grid that contain this primitive\n  locations = []\n  for i in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n    for j in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n      if state.grid[i, j, primitive_index] > 0:\n        locations.append((i, j))\n\n  # If no locations found, return empty list (can't collect)\n  if not locations:\n    return []\n\n  # For now, just return a move to the first location\n  # This is a placeholder - a full implementation would find shortest path and handle obstacles\n  actions = []\n  current_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Simple approach: move towards first found location\n  target = locations[0]\n  if target[0] < current_pos[0]:\n    actions.extend([0] * (current_pos[0] - target[0]))  # Move UP\n  elif target[0] > current_pos[0]:\n    actions.extend([1] * (target[0] - current_pos[0]))  # Move DOWN\n  if target[1] < current_pos[1]:\n    actions.extend([2] * (current_pos[1] - target[1]))  # Move LEFT\n  elif target[1] > current_pos[1]:\n    actions.extend([3] * (target[1] - current_pos[1]))  # Move RIGHT\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
