{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:46:11.011396", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Hint: You might want to use the following helper functions from CraftLab:\n  #   - env.observations() \u2192 dict\n  #   - env.reset(seed=0) \u2192 dict\n  #   - env.step(action, num_steps=1) \u2192 (float, bool, dict)\n  #   - env.action_specs() \u2192 dict\n  #   - env.obs_specs() \u2192 dict\n  #   - env.close() \u2192 None\n\n  # Hint: You might want to use the following helper functions from CraftState:\n  #   - state.next_to(i_kind) \u2192 bool\n  #   - state.satisfies(goal_name, goal_arg) \u2192 bool\n  #   - state.features() \u2192 numpy.ndarray\n  #   - state.features_dict() \u2192 dict\n\n  # Hint: You might want to use the following helper functions from CraftWorld:\n  #   - world.cookbook.primitives_for(goal) \u2192 dict\n  #   - world.grabbable_indices \u2192 list of int indices for entities that can be picked up\n  #   - world.non_grabbable_indices \u2192 set of int indices for entities that cannot be picked up\n  #   - world.workshop_indices \u2192 list of int indices for different types workshop locations\n  #   - world.water_index \u2192 int index for the \u201cwater\u201d entity\n  #   - world.stone_index \u2192 int index for the \u201cstone\u201d entity\n\n  # Hint: You might want to use the following helper functions from CraftScenario:\n  #   - scenario.init() \u2192 CraftState\n\n  # Hint: You might want to use the following helper functions from Cookbook:\n  #   - cookbook.primitives_for(goal) \u2192 dict\n  pass", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:46:12.897139", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # TODO: Implement this function\n  # You can use any functions from the provided code base\n  # The function should return a sequence of actions to collect the specified primitive\n  # You can assume that the environment is static except for changes resulting from tool use\n  # You should only pick up primitives that are passed as the argument\n  # You can use tools already in inventory (e.g., BRIDGE, PICKAXE) but not craft new items\n\n  pass", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:46:44.696926", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if env._current_state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Find all positions that contain the primitive\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  positions = np.where(grid[:,:,primitive_index] > 0)\n  if len(positions[0]) == 0:\n    # Primitive not found in grid, return empty list\n    return []\n  \n  # If the agent is already on a cell containing the primitive, no need to move\n  pos = env._current_state.pos\n  if grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n    # Agent is at the position with the primitive, so just pick it up\n    return [craft.USE]\n  \n  # Otherwise, we need to find a path to reach the primitive\n  # We'll use BFS to find the shortest path\n  from collections import deque\n  queue = deque([(pos[0], pos[1], [])])  # (row, col, actions)\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add(pos)\n\n  # Get possible directions and their corresponding action indices\n  directions = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]  # right, left, down, up\n  action_map = {\n      (0, 1): craft.RIGHT,\n      (0, -1): craft.LEFT,\n      (1, 0): craft.DOWN,\n      (-1, 0): craft.UP\n  }\n\n  while queue:\n    row, col, actions = queue.popleft()\n    \n    for dr, dc in directions:\n      new_row, new_col = row + dr, col + dc\n      \n      # Check if the new position is valid\n      if (new_row < 0 or new_row >= grid.shape[0] or \n          new_col < 0 or new_col >= grid.shape[1]):\n        continue\n        \n      # Check if we've already visited this cell\n      if (new_row, new_col) in visited:\n        continue\n        \n      # Check if the cell is walkable (not a boundary or water)\n      cell_kind = np.argmax(grid[new_row, new_col, :])\n      if cell_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n        continue\n        \n      # Check if we can collect the primitive from this position\n      if grid[new_row, new_col, primitive_index] > 0:\n        # Found the primitive; return the actions to reach it\n        return actions + [action_map[(dr, dc)]]\n        \n      # Add to queue for further exploration\n      visited.add((new_row, new_col))\n      queue.append((new_row, new_col, actions + [action_map[(dr, dc)]]))\n\n  # If we get here, no path was found\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:46:46.617789", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  if env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]] > 0:\n    return []\n  \n  # Find all positions that contain the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  positions = np.where(grid[:,:,primitive_index] > 0)\n  if len(positions[0]) == 0:\n    # Primitive not found in grid, return empty list\n    return []\n  \n  # If the agent is already on a cell containing the primitive, no need to move\n  pos = env._current_state.pos\n  if grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n    # Agent is at the position with the primitive, so just pick it up\n    return [craft.USE]\n  \n  # Otherwise, we need to find a path to reach the primitive\n  # We'll use BFS to find the shortest path\n  from collections import deque\n  queue = deque([(pos[0], pos[1], [])])  # (row, col, actions)\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add(pos)\n\n  # Get possible directions and their corresponding action indices\n  directions = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]  # right, left, down, up\n  action_map = {\n      (0, 1): craft.RIGHT,\n      (0, -1): craft.LEFT,\n      (1, 0): craft.DOWN,\n      (-1, 0): craft.UP\n  }\n\n  while queue:\n    row, col, actions = queue.popleft()\n    \n    for dr, dc in directions:\n      new_row, new_col = row + dr, col + dc\n      \n      # Check if the new position is valid\n      if (new_row < 0 or new_row >= grid.shape[0] or \n          new_col < 0 or new_col >= grid.shape[1]):\n        continue\n        \n      # Check if we've already visited this cell\n      if (new_row, new_col) in visited:\n        continue\n        \n      # Check if the cell is walkable (not a boundary or water)\n      cell_kind = np.argmax(grid[new_row, new_col, :])\n      if cell_kind in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n        continue\n        \n      # Check if we can collect the primitive from this position\n      if grid[new_row, new_col, primitive_index] > 0:\n        # Found the primitive; return the actions to reach it\n        return actions + [action_map[(dr, dc)]]\n        \n      # Add to queue for further exploration\n      visited.add((new_row, new_col))\n      queue.append((new_row, new_col, actions + [action_map[(dr, dc)]]))\n\n  # If we get here, no path was found\n  return []", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:47:08.324515", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the primitive in the environment\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n  if env._current_state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return []\n  \n  # If not, find a path to collect it\n  actions = []\n  # We will use a simple BFS approach to find the shortest path\n  queue = collections.deque([env._current_state.pos])\n  visited = set()\n  parent = {}\n  found = False\n\n  while queue and not found:\n      current_pos = queue.popleft()\n      if current_pos in visited:\n          continue\n      visited.add(current_pos)\n      \n      # Check if the primitive is at this position\n      grid_value = env._current_state.grid[current_pos[0], current_pos[1]]\n      if grid_value[primitive_index] > 0:\n          found = True\n          break\n      \n      # Explore neighbors (up, down, left, right)\n      for dx, dy in [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]:\n          new_pos = (current_pos[0] + dx, current_pos[1] + dy)\n          if (new_pos[0] >= 0 and new_pos[0] < env.world.cookbook.index._len__ and \n              new_pos[1] >= 0 and new_pos[1] < env.world.cookbook.index._len__ and\n              new_pos not in visited):\n              queue.append(new_pos)\n              parent[new_pos] = current_pos\n\n  if found:\n      # Reconstruct path\n      path = []\n      current = current_pos\n      while current != env._current_state.pos:\n          path.append(current)\n          current = parent[current]\n      path.append(env._current_state.pos)\n      path.reverse()\n      \n      # Convert path to actions\n      for i in range(len(path) - 1):\n          current_pos = path[i]\n          next_pos = path[i + 1]\n          \n          if next_pos[0] > current_pos[0]:\n              actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          elif next_pos[0] < current_pos[0]:\n              actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n          elif next_pos[1] > current_pos[1]:\n              actions.append(0)  # DOWN\n          elif next_pos[1] < current_pos[1]:\n              actions.append(1)  # UP\n\n      # Add pickup action at the end\n      actions.append(4)  # USE (pickup)\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:52:08.524210", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # This is a placeholder implementation. Replace this with your own code.\n  actions_to_take = []\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  state = env._current_state\n  print(\"Primitive index:\", primitive_idx)\n  print(\"Current position:\", state.pos)\n  print(\"Inventory:\", state.inventory)\n  print(\"Grid shape:\", state.grid.shape)\n  print(\"Grid content at current pos:\", state.grid[state.pos[0], state.pos[1]])\n  \n  # Check if we already have the primitive\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n    print(\"Already have the primitive\")\n    return actions_to_take\n\n  # Find all cells with the primitive in the grid\n  found_positions = []\n  for x in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n    for y in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n      if state.grid[x, y, primitive_idx] > 0:\n        found_positions.append((x, y))\n  \n  print(\"Found positions:\", found_positions)\n  \n  # If no primitive found, we need to craft it first\n  if not found_positions:\n    print(\"Primitive not found in grid, need to craft\")\n    return actions_to_take\n  \n  # For now, let's just try to move towards the first found position\n  target_pos = found_positions[0]\n  print(\"Target position:\", target_pos)\n  \n  # Simple pathfinding logic - move towards target\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  while current_pos != target_pos:\n    actions_to_take.append(env.action_specs()[\"RIGHT\"])\n    current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] + 1)\n  \n  print(\"Actions to take:\", actions_to_take)\n  return actions_to_take", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T18:52:38.911880", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # TODO: Implement this function.\n  # You can use any of the functions and classes defined in the codebase.\n  # The function should return a list of actions to collect the specified primitive.\n  # If the primitive is already in inventory, return empty list.\n  # If the primitive is a recipe output (i.e., needs crafting), return empty list.\n  # Do not use any functions or classes not defined in the codebase.\n\n  prim_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if env._current_state.inventory[prim_index] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # If the primitive is a recipe output (i.e., needs crafting), return empty list.\n  if prim_index in env.world.cookbook.recipes:\n    return []\n\n  pos = env._current_state.pos\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n\n  queue = collections.deque([(pos, [])])\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add(pos)\n\n  directions = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]  # UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT\n\n  while queue:\n    current_pos, actions = queue.popleft()\n    x, y = current_pos\n\n    if grid[x, y, prim_index] > 0:\n      return actions\n\n    for i, (dx, dy) in enumerate(directions):\n      new_x, new_y = x + dx, y + dy\n      new_pos = (new_x, new_y)\n\n      if not (0 <= new_x < grid.shape[0] and 0 <= new_y < grid.shape[1]):\n        continue\n\n      if new_pos in visited:\n        continue\n\n      # Check traversability.\n      is_traversable = True\n      for kind_idx in range(len(env.world.cookbook.index)):\n        if grid[new_x, new_y, kind_idx] > 0 and kind_idx in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n          is_traversable = False\n          break\n\n      if is_traversable:\n        visited.add(new_pos)\n        queue.append((new_pos, actions + [i]))\n\n  return []", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
