{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T22:28:01.344375", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  state = env._current_state\n  idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  if state.inventory[idx] > 0:\n    return []\n\n  # Check if we are next to the primitive\n  if state.next_to(idx):\n    actions = []\n    # Find the direction to the primitive and move there\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        if abs(dx) + abs(dy) == 1:  # adjacent cells\n          x, y = state.pos[0] + dx, state.pos[1] + dy\n          if (0 <= x < env.world.cookbook.n_kinds and \n              0 <= y < env.world.cookbook.n_kinds):\n            if state.grid[x, y, idx] > 0:\n              # Found the primitive, move to it\n              if dx == -1:\n                actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n              elif dx == 1:\n                actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n              elif dy == -1:\n                actions.append(0)  # UP\n              elif dy == 1:\n                actions.append(1)  # DOWN\n              actions.append(4)  # USE\n              return actions\n\n  # Placeholder: return a sequence of moves towards the primitive\n  # In a real implementation, this would use BFS to find the shortest path\n  # For now, move in some direction (e.g., UP)\n  return [0]  # Default to moving UP", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.5}}
